pe":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":680,"closed_issues":22796,"state":"open","created_at":"2018-01-18T16:52:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T06:25:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":3,"created_at":"2019-04-18T00:46:26Z","updated_at":"2019-09-15T09:52:01Z","closed_at":"2019-05-30T17:34:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description\r\n\r\nThe documentation for ng-deep states\r\n\r\n> Component styles normally apply only to the HTML in the component's own template.\r\n> \r\n> Use the /deep/ shadow-piercing descendant combinator to force a style down through the child component tree into all the child component views. The /deep/ combinator works to any depth of nested components, and it applies to both the view children and content children of the component.\r\n\r\nThis is misleading because styles affected by `::ng-deep` don't only affect \"child component views\"- they affect _all views globally_. \r\n\r\nIt would be more accurate to say that `::ng-deep` turns off view-encapsulation for that style declaration such that it becomes a global style.\r\n\r\n### What's the affected URL?**\r\nhttps://angular.io/guide/component-styles#deprecated-deep--and-ng-deep","closed_by":{"login":"matsko","id":93018,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzMDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93018?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matsko","html_url":"https://github.com/matsko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matsko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matsko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matsko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matsko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users